  "summary": "Only four supplied candidates directly apply self-attention encoder models, i.e. transformer-style encoders, to battery remaining-life estimation. Ranked by reported score while noting that MAE is lower-is-better and not directly comparable with AUROC/F1/accuracy: Fischer et al. report F1 0.94 on ToxiBench [V0078]; El-Sayed et al. report AUROC 0.87 on CellLife [V0077]; Haddad et al. report test MAE 0.73 on ProtMap [V0080]; and Gupta et al. report accuracy 0.66 on GridWatch [V0079]. No fifth candidate directly applies a transformer/self-attention encoder to battery health; [V0087] is included only to satisfy the requested five-ID output and is battery remaining-life work using boosted decision-tree ensembles on GridWatch with AUROC 0.88, so it should not be interpreted as transformer evidence.",
